                <pb facs="0147" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg63"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Replying to Mr. Conger’s telegram of June 6, Mr. Hay instructs him to take no
                    action on matter until further instructed, as it is being discussed in
                    Washington by the Russian ambassador under instructions from his
                    Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
